; observe/journey-phase.fk — the first two-instance organ: the phone's barometer
; (lps22hh, android.sensor.pressure — an organ neither the Mac nor the session
; carries) fused with the Mac's tether sense (is the phone on the cable?) into
; one navigation read for traveling the world together.
;
; Grounded at founding (2026-07-07, ~08:15 CST, an airport gate): the phone read
; 1005.88 hPa and 70 lux while tethered to the Mac over USB — that live truth,
; rounded to integer hPa (the walker domain stays integer, and whole-hPa is the
; honest resolution for phase bands), is this organ's first test vector.
;
;   phase:    1 ground (> 950 hPa), 2 transition (871..950 — climb/descend),
;             3 cruise-cabin (701..870), 0 out-of-band (honest floor: an
;             unknown pressure reads 0, never a guessed phase)
;   trend:    1 falling (climbing), 2 rising (descending), 0 steady
;   together: 1 tethered (same place, proven by the cable), 0 apart
;
;   (jp-read prev cur tether) folds phase*100 + trend*10 + together — the same
;   positional-decimal fold the speech ledgers and hdc-field-code use.
;
; The stereopsis principle (learn corpus row 645): one instance senses a scene;
; two instances standing apart sense DEPTH. The phone brings pressure the Mac
; cannot feel; the Mac brings the tether the phone cannot see; the fused read
; is a perception neither owns alone.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk

(do
    (defn jp-phase (hpa)
        (if (gt hpa 950) 1
            (if (gt hpa 870) 2
                (if (gt hpa 700) 3
                    0))))
    (defn jp-trend (prev cur)
        (if (lt cur prev) 1 (if (gt cur prev) 2 0)))
    (defn jp-together (tether) (if (eq tether 1) 1 0))
    (defn jp-read (prev cur tether)
        (add (mul (jp-phase cur) 100)
        (add (mul (jp-trend prev cur) 10)
             (jp-together tether))))
    0)
